          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\{3,6,9,12\\}\\\\B&=\\{7,8,9,10,11,12\\}\\\\A\\cap B&=\\{9,12\\}\\end{align*}$$\nEach of the 12 outcomes is equally likely.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=\\frac4{12}=\\frac13\\\\P(B)&=\\frac6{12}=\\frac12\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac2{12}=\\frac16\\\\P(A)P(B)&=\\frac13\\times\\frac12=\\frac16\\end{align*}$$\nSince $P(A\\cap B)=P(A)P(B)$, $A$ and $B$ are independent.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
